diff --git a/docs/development.md b/docs/development.md
index 0bca076..8a2ddaa 100644
--- a/docs/development.md
+++ b/docs/development.md
@@ -72,8 +72,21 @@ bin/rails dev:email
 
 Under the hood, this will create or remove `tmp/email-dev.txt`.
 
+### Email notification digests
+
+People choose their email frequency in **Notification Settings**. The setting
+`bundle_email_frequency` defaults to `never` (off); `every_few_hours`, `daily`, and
+`weekly` collect notifications for four hours, one day, and one week respectively.
+
+Each window starts when its first notification arrives, rather than at a fixed
+time of day. Late notifications join the open window. Changing frequency affects
+the next window without resizing an existing one; switching off also suppresses
+pending digests. Delivery runs through the background job queue, with a recurring
+sweep to recover overdue windows.
+
 ## SaaS gem
 
+
 37signals bundles Fizzy with [`fizzy-saas`](https://github.com/basecamp/fizzy/tree/main/saas), a companion gem that links Fizzy with our billing system and contains our production setup.
 
 This gem depends on some private git repositories and it is not meant to be used by third parties. But we hope it can serve as inspiration for anyone wanting to run fizzy on their own infrastructure.
